; Generated by scripts/generate-flt-modular-inverses.py; checked native proof terms.
; Every nonzero canonical residue at an actual prime is coprime.
; Its computed inverse satisfies both product laws and is nonzero.
; Prime evidence and the distinction from composite nonunits remain
; explicit; the zero-modulus integer branch is not a finite field.
(#alias symmetry = ./equality.lim::symmetry)
